{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Button-Activated Viewport Drawing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Button-Activated Viewport Drawing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"button activated viewport drawing button activated viewport drawing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Button-Activated Viewport Drawing.md","fileName":"Button-Activated Viewport Drawing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Button-Activated Viewport Drawing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Viewport Drawing API]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Viewport Drawing API","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Button-Activated Viewport Drawing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Button-Activated Viewport Drawing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"button activated viewport drawing button activated viewport drawing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Button-Activated Viewport Drawing.md","fileName":"Button-Activated Viewport Drawing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Button-Activated Viewport Drawing","heading":"Button-Activated Viewport Drawing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A Blender operator can toggle a viewport draw handler in response to a panel button. When the overlay is inactive, execution adds the handler and stores its reference; when active, execution removes it and clears the reference. A window-level Boolean can keep the panel's displayed state consistent with the actual handler.\n\nThis lifecycle solves a problem with one-off scripts: a persistent draw callback may otherwise remain attached until Blender restarts. The button gives the user control, while unregistration provides a final cleanup path if the add-on is disabled during drawing.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Viewport Drawing API","b